        "The particle model explains the three states: in solids, particles vibrate about fixed positions in an ordered lattice; in liquids they are close but disordered and slide past one another; in gases they are far apart and move randomly at high speed. Rising temperature increases average particle energy. This single picture accounts for fixed shape in solids, fixed volume in liquids and compressibility in gases, and it is the backbone of {S}.",
