        "Security and industry use radiation daily: cargo scanners at the ports, level gauges in bottling plants, weld testing on pipelines with gamma sources. Archaeologists date charcoal from ancient settlements with carbon-14, and geologists date basement rocks with uranium-lead. Each application pairs a nuclide with a half-life matched to the task, a selection rule {S} teaches.",
