        "Half-life arithmetic fails when students subtract days linearly instead of halving per interval, or halve the mass but not the count rate, which must follow identically. Confusing the mass number changes of alpha and beta decay is another classic. Writing the successive-halving table is the {S} habit that prevents both.",
